    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"lost_negative_case\",\"target_kind\":\"omission\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that policy debate is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_f2a201946e7ca8c8\",\"quote\":\"I wish you a happy new year, Mr Speaker Plymouth’s Charles Cross police station reputedly has England’s busiest custody suite. ...\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_95b193c9b4e6e362\",\"quote\":\"As my hon. Friend will know, the provision of mental health nurses in police custody suites is a local issue...\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_dd63d66bb1b0c365\",\"quote\":\"It is clearly good news that the number of people detained overnight in police stations under the Mental Health Act has been reduced by 25%...\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_5c27013bca8aec13\",\"quote\":\"I am grateful to my hon. Friend for pointing out the success of the work already being done...\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_dd63d66bb1b0c365\",\"quote\":\"Clearly, it is important that individuals who are ill need to be treated medically, rather than be detained in police stations.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"absence of discussion regarding the potential for policy debate to be driven by factors other than institutional procedures and paperwork\",\"mechanism\":\"Omission of a key counterargument\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim presents an incomplete picture of policy debate drivers, ignoring other relevant influences.\",\"counterconditions\":\"No evidence exists to suggest that the sources explicitly address alternative drivers of policy debate.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The evidence demonstrates a focus on NHS commissioning and reduced detentions, neglecting broader policy considerations and the role of diverse stakeholders in driving debate.\"}",
    "done": true,
